tests/ui/check/ok_equation.sky:4:1: note: `sky run` runs this program on the tree-walking interpreter, not as native code: differential equations are not supported by SIR yet
  |
4 | equation orbit(t: s):
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

tests/ui/check/ok_equation.sky:10:7: note: `orbit` is a second-order system, so a symplectic integrator applies
   |
10 | sol = solve orbit from 0 s to 1 yr with r = [1 AU, 0 m], v = [0 m/s, 29.8 km/s]:
   |       ^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: `r' = v`, and the accelerations depend only on `t` and the positions, not on the velocities
   = note: tolerance: 1e-9
   = note: to be conserved: `energy`; the solver monitors the drift of each and reports it
   = note: the method is chosen when the program runs; `print(explain(sol))` says which, and why

tests/ui/check/ok_equation.sky:22:5: note: `decay` is a general first-order system
   |
22 | d = solve decay from 0 s to 4 s with n = 1
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: the equations of `decay` have no second-order structure (no `q' = v` with `v'` free of `v`), so only general-purpose methods apply
   = note: no tolerance given: the solver's default applies
   = note: the method is chosen when the program runs; `print(explain(sol))` says which, and why
